                </div><div class="detail-main_body" id="content">
                  <div class="detail-main_rich-text w-richtext">
                    <h2>‍<strong>Overview</strong></h2><p>
                      GoStops didn't plan to become India's largest hostel brand. The idea came from
                      a trip to Europe in 2012, when co-founder Pankaj Parwanda found himself in a
                      Bob Marley hostel, and within five minutes, strangers were sharing their
                      stories across a barstool. His wife Pallavi made the call: someone should
                      build this for India. That was the beginning of GoStops.
                    </p><p>
                      Now GoStops operates hostels across 30+ properties, serving travellers who are
                      searching for connection, not just a bed. The business is operationally
                      intensive by nature. Every property runs its own vendor relationships,
                      maintenance contracts, housekeeping services, repair work, utility bills.
                    </p><h2><strong>The Challenge</strong></h2><h3>
                      <strong>Bills arrived from everywhere</strong>
                    </h3><p>
                      Every bill from across 30 properties made its way to the finance team over
                      email or Google Drive. Some arrived couriered  paper documents that someone at
                      HQ had to physically open, read, and enter. The process of getting a bill from
                      a property into the books was a multi-step, multi-person task that the finance
                      team had no system for. It was, in Nikhil's words, "a task to perform."
                    </p><h3><strong>Manual Reconciliation</strong></h3><p>
                      The reconciliation that followed was the most time-consuming part. At every
                      book-closing cycle, the team worked through a backlog of entries that needed
                      to be matched, verified, and accounted for. The process was slow not because
                      the team was underperforming, but because the inputs were scattered and the
                      tools weren't built for this volume.
                    </p><h3><strong>Payment authorisation was a nightly interruption</strong></h3><p
                    >
                      Pankaj is the payment authoriser, so whenever the payments team submitted
                      transactions  often at nine o'clock at night  he had to open his laptop, open
                      the bank app on a separate phone, and navigate a rotating OTP that expired
                      every 60 seconds. The race between remembering the password and the phone
                      screen dimming was a nightly occurrence.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "Usually I would just get very irritated. The payments team will just input
                      payments at 9 o'clock in the night and that will mean me opening my laptop,
                      another phone, opening the bank app, and that would sort of rotate a password
                      every 60 secs... I think it was enough stress." ~ Pankaj Parwanda, Co-Founder,
                      goSTOPs
                    </blockquote><h2><strong>The Solution</strong></h2><h3>
                      <strong>Centralised bill ingestion</strong>
                    </h3><p>
                      With Mysa, every invoice  regardless of which property it originated from, and
                      regardless of whether it arrived over email or was uploaded directly,. flows
                      into a single system. The finance team no longer receives bills piecemeal from
                      30 inboxes. Mysa picks up the invoice, fills all the data, and holds it at the
                      review point. Nikhil's team goes into one place, verifies the details, and
                      moves it forward to payment or accounting.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "Mysa automatically picks up the invoice from email, fill all the data. So I
                      just go and verify the details and then proceed for payment or for
                      accounting."  Nikhil Aggarwal, AVP Finance, GoStops
                    </blockquote><h3><strong>Payment Authorization from Mobile</strong></h3><p>
                      Pankaj now authorises payments easily from the Mysa mobile app. He can now
                      select 100 payments and authorise, with full bill context.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "Now if they just input, even while driving actually at a red light, I'm able
                      to select 100 payments and just approve."  Pankaj Parwanda, Co-Founder,
                      goSTOPs
                    </blockquote><p>
                      The payments team noticed immediately. goSTOPs runs a lean authorisation
                      structure, and the friction that used to sit between a submitted payment and
                      an authorised one is gone.
                    </p><h3><strong>Spend analytics by room</strong></h3><p>
                      Because every payment in Mysa is tagged with the relevant property, room
                      number, and cost centre at the point of entry, GoStops now has enough
                      granularity to catch the pattern that was previously invisible.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "Today because it's being inputted with the room number, there is enough
                      analytics available, it clearly throws out that there is an AC in room 201
                      that is undergoing repeated issues, and that sort of helps us get such minute
                      issues highlighted."  Pankaj Parwanda, Co-Founder, GoStops
                    </blockquote><p>
                      <em>See how Mysa's </em><a href="/reports-and-insights"
                        ><em>Reports and Insights</em></a
                      ><em> surface spend data by cost centre in real time.</em>
                    </p><h3><strong>Faster Book Closing</strong></h3><p>
                      The reconciliation task that used to consume book-closing cycles is now
                      handled by the platform. Mysa's <a href="/zoho-books-integration"
                        >Zoho integration</a
                      > means payment entries are automatically passed through and matched  no manual
                      portal entries, no data entry tasks for the finance team to complete before they
                      can start closing. What used to take two to three additional working days just
                      for reconciliation has been reclaimed.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "We saw book closing time reduce by 2-3 working days just on account of
                      reconciliation, so I have 3 hours quality time of my team daily."  Nikhil
                      Aggarwal, AVP Finance, GoStops
                    </blockquote><p>
                      For Nikhil's team of two to three people who were previously spending a large
                      part of their day on transactional reconciliation work, those hours now go
                      toward analysis and decision support. The clerical layer has come down. The
                      finance team's output has gone up.
                    </p><p>
                      <em>See how Mysa's </em><a href="/audit-trails"><em>Audit Trails</em></a><em>
                        make every bill, approval, and payment traceable without manual
                        reconstruction.</em>
                    </p><h3><strong>Seamless Accounting Sync</strong></h3><p>
                      One of the features Nikhil highlights is the Zoho integration. Vendors created
                      in Mysa's accounting module are automatically created in Zoho. Payment entries
                      pass through Mysa into the books. The reconciliation that used to be a
                      month-end scramble now happens as a byproduct of how payments are processed.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "One of the best parts about Mysa is the seamless integration with Zoho. My
                      vendors get auto-created in Zoho, if I create in Mysa."  Nikhil Aggarwal, AVP
                      Finance, GoStops
                    </blockquote><h3>
                      <strong>Support that is available when the business needs it</strong>
                    </h3><p>
                      GoStops describes Mysa's support as a differentiator in how they chose and
                      stayed with the platform. The entire team is on a WhatsApp group. When a
                      payment issue comes up  even one involving 100 payments going through with one
                      flagged  Pankaj doesn't write a support ticket and wait two days for a
                      response. Someone responds, and if needed, gets on a call.
                    </p><blockquote>
                      "There's someone to respond to even in the middle of the night."  Pankaj
                      Parwanda, Co-Founder, goSTOPs
                    </blockquote><h2><strong>Looking Forward</strong></h2><p>
                      Pankaj has discussed processing payments through virtual cards with the
                      product team. The potential he sees in Mysa is as a complete AP tool: that
                      handles the procurement process from PO through to payment, while keeping
                      inventory visibility intact. For a multi-property hospitality business where
                      procurement and maintenance are constant, that kind of end-to-end capability
                      is the next layer GoStops wants to build on.
                    </p>
